t that flap pop  out from the back line up this outside  edge with the middle and then you could  push down here  very gently then you could lift up this  flap and crease on this edge here so now  you should have something that looks  like this  now we could flip over the model again  and you'll see we have this pocket here  on the back what we're going to do is  we're going to take these edges here on  the bottom now and we're going to fold  them directly on to the midline so you  want to take this corner and fold it  inwards until this bottom edge is lined  up directly with the middle of the paper  like that fold it in and once it's lined  up in the middle make a crease on the  outside just like that  do the same with the left side so just  line up this edge with the middle  so you should have something that looks  like this this next step of making the  origami beating hardest probably the  trickiest one but I'm going to go  through it slowly and in a lot of detail  to make it easier to understand if  you've made the crane or the gift box  you'll see this is very similar to the  petal fold there's a few different ways  we can do it a little bit easier first  I'd like you to draw a line from this  corner of this diamond to the opposite  corner just as I've drawn there also you  want to make these edges here a little  bit sharper so just take your fingernail  and run it against those creases here to  make them very sharp now you can unfold  these two edges from the center and then  what we're going to do is we're going to  open up this pocket here and you want to  push on this line all the way across so  it should kind of crease on that line  there and what you're going to do is  you're going to take your finger and  you're going to push this edge of the  paper all the way up here just like this  and you'll see when we do that these  edges here will start to go inwards  towards the middle so you want to make  sure it's creasing on that line that you  drew push all 